{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"coyish-fluent-gibbon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Store accepts secret-bearing event bodies; leak blocked all tickets pushes\n\n## Summary\n\nAt 2026-08-03 19:13 an agent session posted a comment on ticket 129e containing a full zsh environment dump. The dump embedded SEVEN live credentials (Anthropic, 2x GitHub PAT, Gemini/Google, Jira/Atlassian, OpenAI service-account, PyPI). GitHub push protection then rejected refs/heads/tickets (GH013) on the Anthropic key, so EVERY session's store writes queued local-only (153 commits at diagnosis) — a full store-sharing outage triggered by one comment.\n\nrebar has no write-time secret guard: `comment`/`edit`/event append accept arbitrary bodies, and the auto-push seam surfaces the rejection only as `WARNING rebar._store.push: tickets branch push failed after 3 retries`, which names neither the offending commit nor the reason, so the outage looks like transient contention.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. No secret-pattern screening at the event-write seam (comment/description/session-log bodies).\n2. The push-retry path swallows the git error detail (GH013 + secret location were only visible via a manual `git push`).\n\n## Fix plan\n\n1. Add a deterministic secret screen at the event-append seam (single choke point all writers share): reject or redact bodies matching high-confidence credential patterns (sk-ant-*, ghp_/gho_/ghu_/ghs_/ghr_, github_pat_, AIza…, ATATT…, xox?-, AKIA…, pypi-AgE…, sk-proj-/sk-svcacct-, PEM private-key headers) BEFORE the event file is written. Reject with a teaching message (what matched, why, how to redact); `--allow-secret-pattern=<reason>` style override deliberately NOT provided over MCP.\n2. Surface push-rejection detail: when the store push fails, include the git stderr tail (first GH013 violation line + path) in the warning so the failure self-identifies.\n3. Unit tests: each pattern fires; placeholder/regex-text forms (e.g. `sk-ant-api03-...`, `sk-ant-api03-[A-Za-z0-9_-]`) do NOT fire (word-boundary + length guards — the store already contains such benign strings in jira-reb-687 REVIEW_RESULT events); redaction path preserves event schema; push-failure warning carries the reason.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Event-append rejects (or redacts, per config) bodies matching the high-confidence credential patterns, with a teaching message naming the matched pattern class.\n- [ ] Placeholder/truncated forms and pattern-literals in review payloads do not trip the screen (regression fixtures from jira-reb-687 events).\n- [ ] Store push failures log the git rejection reason (GH013 line + offending path) instead of a bare retry count.\n- [ ] Unit tests cover fire/no-fire per pattern and the enriched push warning.\n\n## File impact\n\n- src/rebar (event-append seam; store push module) — exact modules to be pinned during planning with Serena/grep.\n- tests/unit (new secret-screen suite; push-warning test).","id":"e7a9-35fa-1d58-4095","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Store accepts secret-bearing event bodies; leak blocked all tickets pushes"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785818313332875001,"uuid":"9605cf3e-5f41-4516-98d2-5af436e9bbcc"}